  "vulnerability_information": "## Summary\n\nWith a `CURLSH` sharing `CURL_LOCK_DATA_CONNECT` attached to an easy handle, libcurl creates the handle for an HTTP/2 server-pushed stream internally via `h2_duphandle()` → `curl_easy_duphandle()` (`lib/http2.c`). `curl_easy_duphandle()` does not copy `->share`, so that handle has `share == NULL`. `Curl_multi_add_perform()` then attaches it to the parent's connection, which is pooled in `share->cpool`.\n\nWhen the pushed transfer ends, `cpool_get_instance()` resolves the pool from the handle:\n`share == NULL` yields `multi->cpool`, not the `share->cpool` that owns the connection.\n`cpool_remove_conn()` does not find the connection, so it is freed while still linked in\n`share->cpool`'s bundle (`bits.in_cpool` remains TRUE). A later walk of `share->cpool`\ndereferences the freed `connectdata`.\n\nCWE-416 (use-after-free).\n\n## Affected versions\n\n* **curl 8.21.0** (tag `curl-8_21_0`).\n* **master `2112f185c`** (2026-08-04, libcurl 8.22.0-DEV) — reproduces 3/3.\n\nState of the three sites at `2112f185c`:\n\n| site | state |\n|---|---|\n| `h2_duphandle` — `lib/http2.c:699` | calls `curl_easy_duphandle(data)`; `share` occurs 0 times in `lib/http2.c` |\n| `curl_easy_duphandle` — `lib/easy.c:970` | does not copy `->share` |\n| `cpool_get_instance` — `lib/conncache.c:256` | resolves the pool from the handle, not the connection |\n\n## Reproduction\n\n`repro.c` (attached) is standalone pure libcurl: an in-process thread serves raw h2c frames\nover a socketpair via `CURLOPT_OPENSOCKETFUNCTION` + `CURL_SOCKOPT_ALREADY_CONNECTED`. No\nnetwork, no server, no TLS. It creates a `CURLSH` sharing `CURL_LOCK_DATA_CONNECT`, runs an\nHTTP/2 transfer, accepts a `PUSH_PROMISE` (`CURL_PUSH_OK`), and the server sends `GOAWAY`.\n\nBuilt against a release (`ENABLE_DEBUG=OFF`) + ASan libcurl:\n\n```sh\ncmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=RelWithDebInfo -DENABLE_DEBUG=OFF \\\n  -DBUILD_SHARED_LIBS=OFF -DBUILD_CURL_EXE=OFF -DBUILD_TESTING=OFF \\\n  -DCURL_USE_OPENSSL=OFF -DUSE_NGHTTP2=ON -DCURL_USE_LIBPSL=OFF -DUSE_LIBIDN2=OFF \\\n  -DCURL_BROTLI=OFF -DCURL_ZSTD=OFF \\\n  -DCMAKE_C_FLAGS=\"-fsanitize=address -g -fno-omit-frame-pointer\"\ncmake --build build && cmake --install build\n\ncc -fsanitize=address -g repro.c -o repro -I<prefix>/include \\\n   <prefix>/lib/libcurl.a -lnghttp2 -lz -lpthread -ldl\nASAN_OPTIONS=detect_leaks=0 ./repro\n```\n\nResult: heap-use-after-free, 3/3 runs, on both curl 8.21.0 and master `2112f185c`.\n\nIn a `DEBUGBUILD` libcurl the inconsistency aborts earlier at `DEBUGASSERT(NULL)`\n`lib/conncache.c:179` (\"Should have been in the bundle list\") instead of reaching the free.\n\n## AddressSanitizer output (master `2112f185c`, release + ASan)\n\n`READ of size 8` into a freed 776-byte `connectdata` (the struct was 832 bytes in 8.21.0).\nFull log: `asan-retest-master-2026-08-04.txt`.\n\n```\nREAD of size 8:\n  Curl_node_elem            lib/llist.c:237\n  cpool_get_first           lib/conncache.c:142\n  Curl_cpool_destroy        lib/conncache.c:242\n  share_destroy             lib/curl_share.c:41\n  curl_share_cleanup        lib/curl_share.c:370\n\nfreed by:\n  Curl_cshutdn_terminate    lib/cshutdn.c:159\n  cpool_discard_conn        lib/conncache.c:226\n  Curl_conn_terminate       lib/conncache.c:692\n  Curl_cpool_do_locked      lib/conncache.c:833\n  multi_done                lib/multi.c:750\n  multi_handle_timeout      lib/multi.c:1848\n  multi_runsingle           lib/multi.c:2757\n  multi_perform             lib/multi.c:2888\n\npreviously allocated by:\n  allocate_conn             lib/url.c:1182\n  url_create_needle         lib/url.c:2010\n  url_find_or_create_conn   lib/url.c:2250\n  Curl_connect              lib/url.c:2456\n```\n\n`verifynode()` (`lib/llist.c:36`) is `DEBUGBUILD`-only; in a release build the read lands at\n`Curl_node_elem()`.\n\n## Root cause\n\n1. `curl_easy_duphandle()` does not copy `->share` (`docs/libcurl/curl_easy_duphandle.md`:\n   the clone is \"created as if `CURLOPT_SHARE` was set to NULL\").\n2. `push_promise()` → `h2_duphandle()` → `curl_easy_duphandle()` ⇒ pushed handle has\n   `share == NULL`.\n3. `push_promise()` → `Curl_multi_add_perform(data->multi, newhandle, cf->conn)` →\n   `Curl_attach_connection(newhandle, cf->conn)` ⇒ the pushed handle holds the parent's\n   connection, which is in `share->cpool`.\n4. `cpool_get_instance(data)` (`lib/conncache.c:256`) returns `&data->share->cpool` only when\n   `CURL_SHARE_KEEP_CONNECT(data->share)`; for the pushed handle it returns `multi->cpool`.\n5. `multi_done()` → `Curl_cpool_do_locked()` → `Curl_conn_terminate()` →\n   `cpool_remove_conn(multi->cpool, conn)`: the connection is not in that pool, so it is not\n   unlinked and `bits.in_cpool` stays TRUE.\n6. `cpool_discard_conn()` → `Curl_cshutdn_terminate()` frees the `connectdata`.\n7. `curl_share_cleanup()` → `share_destroy()` → `Curl_cpool_destroy()` → `cpool_get_first()` → `Curl_node_elem()` reads the freed `connectdata`.\n\n## Trigger\n\nApplication setup, all before the transfer starts:\n\n```c\nCURLSH *sh = curl_share_init();\ncurl_share_setopt(sh, CURLSHOPT_SHARE, CURL_LOCK_DATA_CONNECT);\ncurl_easy_setopt(easy, CURLOPT_SHARE, sh);\ncurl_multi_setopt(multi, CURLMOPT_PUSHFUNCTION, push_cb);  /* returns CURL_PUSH_OK */\n```\n\nThe push callback returns `CURL_PUSH_OK` and calls no libcurl function. No option or share is modified after the transfer starts. Single-threaded. The pushed-stream handle is created by libcurl, not by the application.\n\nServer side: send `PUSH_PROMISE`, then end the pushed stream before it completes. The attached reproducer uses `GOAWAY`. `RST_STREAM`, connection close, `CURLOPT_TIMEOUT_MS` expiry, and `curl_multi_remove_handle()` of the pushed handle all reach `multi_done()` → `Curl_conn_terminate()` with the share-less handle.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nPropagate the parent's share to the pushed handle in `h2_duphandle()`/`push_promise()` before `Curl_multi_add_perform()` (`newhandle->share = data->share;` plus refcount/lock handling), or terminate a connection against the cpool that owns it rather than\n`cpool_get_instance(data)`.\n\n## Attachments\n\n| file | contents |\n|---|---|\n| `repro.c`, `run.sh` | standalone reproducer |\n| `asan-retest-master-2026-08-04.txt` | ASan log, master `2112f185c` |\n| `asan-standalone.txt` | ASan log, 8.21.0 |\n| `asan-recover-master-2026-08-04.txt` | ASan log with `-fsanitize-recover`, showing all three reads |\n| `repro-harness.bin` | original fuzzer input (debug build, asserts at `conncache.c:179`) |\n| `RETEST-2026-08-04.md` | retest method and build details |\n\n## Impact\n\nThe freed `connectdata` stays linked in `share->cpool`'s bundle with `bits.in_cpool` set, so it remains reachable from any subsequent operation on that pool — not only from\n`curl_share_cleanup()`.\n\nMeasured on master `2112f185c` with a release + ASan libcurl built with\n`-fsanitize-recover=address` and run under `ASAN_OPTIONS=halt_on_error=0`, so execution continues past the first error (`asan-recover-master-2026-08-04.txt`):\n\n| # | access | offset into the freed 776-byte region | site |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `READ of size 8` | 8 | `Curl_node_elem` — `lib/llist.c:237` |\n| 2 | `READ of size 8` | 0 | `Curl_node_llist` — `lib/llist.c:269` |\n| 3 | `READ of size 8` | 88 | `cpool_remove_conn` — `lib/conncache.c:169` |\n\nThree reads of freed heap memory at three distinct offsets and three distinct sites. **No\nwrite to the freed region was observed** in that run.\n\nThe connection object is heap-allocated by `allocate_conn()` (`lib/url.c:1182`) and freed by `Curl_cshutdn_terminate()` (`lib/cshutdn.c:159`); the interval between the free and the reads contains further libcurl allocation activity.",
